{"parentUuid":"901fa348-85fa-4d7e-9f40-2497eea5edba","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce5Y1rAz4XJBCZKV79oBT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DnJBbwCdUo7SkyvmX15LRo","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement TASK-12 (AC-12 regression test)","subagent_type":"lambda:lambda-implementer","prompt":"Read task TASK-12 from the plan file at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/plan-track3a-v2.json (a plan@1 object; find the task with id \"TASK-12\" — title \"Regression-proof: AC-12 (consolidated Cargo membership regression group)\"). Execute exactly that one task via the standard TDD cycle (red test confirmed failing, minimal implementation if any is needed, green, commit).\n\nWorkspace manifest context: workspace_root is /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto, language is rust, test runner is `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib`. spec_file_path is .claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK3A-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP.json (34 acceptance criteria — read TASK-12's covers_criteria (AC-12) exact text directly from that spec file before writing the test, don't rely on paraphrased criteria text from the plan). AC-12 is described as a \"consolidated regression group\" — read its exact spec text carefully, it may bundle multiple related sub-behaviors into one criterion rather than a single narrow assertion.\n\nCritical context: this task modifies crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs, the same file TASK-05 through TASK-11 just landed changes to (commits 0971005, d812cac, 8c6de26, 498f27c, 58ae93d, d5d659b, 1e0dc69, all already on the current branch). Start by running `git log --oneline -8 -- crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs` and `git status` to confirm all seven are present and the tree is clean before you begin.\n\nTASK-07 through TASK-11 were all titled \"regression-proof\" and all required no new implementation (behavior already existed from earlier tasks, tests passed immediately). This task may follow the same pattern, or may not — verify by actually running the test yourself, don't assume either way. If the test passes with no red step, adversarially verify it's not vacuous (temporarily break the relevant logic in membership.rs, confirm the test then fails, then restore it) before treating \"no red step\" as legitimate — this precedent from TASK-08/09/10/11 has worked well.\n\nEstablished patterns from this same plan's ~28 prior completed tasks, still applicable:\n- A recurring gotcha on this plan: task notes/prose (failing_test predictions, \"note\" fields, assumptions about prior task state) have repeatedly diverged from actual observed behavior in earlier tasks. Always verify by actually running the test/command yourself, never trust the plan's characterization blindly.\n- `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"` workspace invariant — never introduce unsafe blocks.\n- Run `cargo fmt -p callisto-graph` and `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings` before committing; this repo's pre-commit hook enforces format-check and WILL reject an unformatted commit — if that happens, run `cargo fmt`, re-stage, and create a fresh commit (do not amend).\n- Watch for `clippy::cmp_owned` specifically if your test compares a `PathBuf` — use `Path::new(\"...\")` on the right-hand side of `==` against a `PathBuf`/`&Path`, not `PathBuf::from(\"...\")`. This lint has bitten prior tasks already.\n- Commit per task once green, using the plan's commit_message (or a corrected one if it doesn't match what was actually implemented) — established, user-approved pattern for this pipeline.\n\nReport back: task_id, status, steps_completed, test_result, commit_sha, criteria_evidence (file+line for test and implementation per criterion in covers_criteria), and any concerns/contradictions found."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2