nce\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-09f\",\n      \"test_file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs\",\n      \"test_line\": 1300,\n      \"implementation_file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs\",\n      \"implementation_line\": 12\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-09i\",\n      \"test_file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs\",\n      \"test_line\": 1323,\n      \"implementation_file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs\",\n      \"implementation_line\": 12\n    }\n  ],\n  \"concerns\": null,\n  \"reasoning\": \"Plan's fixture matched the spec's exact criterion text for both AC-09f and AC-09i (same fixture shapes: 'crates/kept-example' + 'crates/[unterminated' for members; 'crates/*' members with exclude=['crates/scratch-example','crates/[unterminated'] for exclude). No missing clauses found in the plan's version this time, unlike some prior tasks. Adapted PathBuf::from(...) in the plan's test code to Path::new(...) per this plan's established clippy::cmp_owned avoidance pattern. No implementation change was needed — build_globset's existing per-entry skip-on-compile-failure logic (crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs:12-19) already satisfies both criteria, proven via mutation-based adversarial check rather than assumed.\"\n}\n```\n\nSummary: Task TASK-22 executed as a regression-proof task (no implementation change needed). Added two tests to `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs` (lines 1300 and 1323) proving AC-09f and AC-09i — both pass against the existing `build_globset` implementation in `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs` (line 12). Since there was no red step, I adversarially verified non-vacuity by temporarily breaking the per-entry skip logic in `build_globset